  "worked_solution": "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14257924/assets/e48f172079d6edc0b29356cafa30c82fcae0afd008e469ea8e0ad9a3660d6fd0.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y+y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles II and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle I covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
